# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for the Sanitizer Tests workflow
# (.github/workflows/sanitizers.yml loads this file through TSAN_OPTIONS).
#
# Only races inside third-party or ecosystem code belong here, each with the
# upstream issue and the condition for removing it. Never suppress
# pacs_system code: a pacs_system test that fails under a sanitizer is
# quarantined in ctest-quarantine-<sanitizer>.txt with its issue instead.

# kcenon/thread_system#761: detail::concurrent_queue publishes node::next
# without release/acquire ordering (enqueue() writes it under tail_mutex_,
# try_dequeue() reads it under head_mutex_), so TSan sees no happens-before
# between producer and consumer. Remove this entry when the thread_system SHA
# pinned in .github/actions/checkout-kcenon-deps contains the fix for #761.
race:kcenon::thread::detail::concurrent_queue
